    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S005",
      "patient_response": "Well, what brings me in is... I just can't seem to keep my work in order anymore. It's a mess. I work at a dry cleaner's, and lately, it's just tickets, receipts, workshop notes, customer jobs—all just piled together until I don't even know what to handle first. It's like looking at a mountain of paper. Speaking of mountains, my sister went to the Rockies last week. She sent me these pictures, and they were just gorgeous. I haven't been on a vacation in... gosh, it must be ten years. We used to go to the beach when the kids were little, but now everyone's so busy. My youngest is trying to start his own landscaping business, actually. He’s got a real green thumb, unlike me. I killed a cactus once. But anyway, yeah, the piles at work. I just... I look at them and my brain just kind of stops.",
