    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "How long have you noticed these difficulties with staying organized and focused?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, it's really been causing me actual trouble for... I'd say about two years and two months now. That's right around when I started changing the business into this more complicated boutique model. Because, you know, regular dry cleaning is one thing, but boutique means we handle high-end stuff. Couture, delicate vintage pieces. I actually had this one lady bring in a 1920s flapper dress last month, and the beading on it was just incredible. All hand-stitched glass beads. I don't know how anyone had the patience for that back then! \n\nPeople today just don't have patience, do they? Everybody wants everything in five minutes. They call it fast fashion. My niece buys all her clothes from those cheap websites on her phone and they just fall apart after one wash. It's a terrible waste, really. She brought me a sweater to try and fix once and the yarn was practically made of plastic. You can't even steam something like that without it melting. \n\nBut, um... what was I saying? Oh, right, the boutique model. Yeah, it just made everything so much more complicated with all the special care instructions and different solvents we have to track, and that's when the piles really started getting completely out of hand for me.",
