    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Did you experience similar problems with focus or disorganization when you were a child or in school?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Well, you know, it's funny you ask that, because... yes, actually. Even way back in grade school. My mother kept all my old report cards in this big cedar chest at the foot of her bed. It smelled so strongly of cedar, you know? I love that smell. It reminds me of the holidays. We used to get a real tree every year until my husband developed this terrible allergy to pine. He'd just sneeze and sneeze until his eyes swelled up. So we had to switch to an artificial one, which just isn't the same. It's pre-lit, which is nice because I hate stringing lights, they always get tangled. \n\nBut, um, my report cards. Right. My teachers always wrote the same thing. They'd tell my mother I was bright, but just... scattered. I was always talking out of turn, losing my homework papers, and they constantly had to remind me to just finish what I was doing. I guess I've always been a bit like that, but it's just so much worse with the business now.",
