    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel restless inside, or find it difficult to sit still without fidgeting?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Well, I don't know if I'd say I feel restless inside, exactly. I mean, I guess I do tap my foot a lot when I'm sitting at the front counter. The stool there is just so uncomfortable. It's one of those wooden ones with no cushion. I keep meaning to bring a pillow from home, but I always forget. I have this lovely needlepoint pillow my aunt made for me years ago. It has a picture of a little yellow canary on it. She loved birds, my aunt. She had three parakeets that used to fly right around her living room. They made such a mess, though, with the seeds everywhere. You'd step on them and they'd crunch into the carpet. \n\nCarpet is so hard to keep clean, don't you think? That's why we put laminate down in our hallway last year. It looks just like real oak, but you can just run a damp mop over it and you're done. My husband installed it himself. He's very handy like that, when his back isn't acting up. He threw it out last spring trying to lift a bag of mulch and was on the sofa for a week. \n\nBut, oh, what were you asking? Fidgeting? I'm not really sure. I just... I like to keep my hands busy, I suppose.",
