    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often find yourself interrupting other people when they are speaking?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S018",
      "patient_response": "Well, I... I suppose I do that, yes. Especially at the shop. I'll just cut right into my staff's conversations, or I'll reach over and start fixing how they're sorting the clothes before they even ask for help. I know it comes off like I'm butting in, but it's just... I see it being done wrong and I have to fix it. \n\nLike yesterday, Sarah was sorting a pile of silks, and she had this beautiful emerald green blouse right next to a rough wool cardigan. You can't do that! The wool will snag the silk in a heartbeat. Silk is so delicate. I had a silk scarf once, a real Hermes one that I found at an estate sale for five dollars. Can you believe it? Five dollars! The woman running the sale clearly had no idea what she had. It had this gorgeous equestrian print on it, all horses and riding crops. I wore it all the time until I accidentally left it in a taxi in Chicago. \n\nChicago is so windy, though, isn't it? We went there for a long weekend a few years ago and I thought I was going to freeze. The pizza was good, though. Deep dish. It's really more like a casserole than a pizza, if you ask me. You need a knife and fork to eat it. \n\nBut, um... interrupting. Right. Yes, I do that. I just can't seem to stop myself from jumping in when I see something that needs fixing or if I just have something to say right then.",
